our architecture is already a good foundation for production, especially because you're separating semantic retrieval (Qdrant) from structural retrieval (Neo4j). The biggest opportunity is to avoid making every query go through expensive multi-query + graph + reranking, because that increases latency and tokens without necessarily improving results.

I would evolve it toward a hybrid, adaptive retrieval architecture.

