Priority of upgrades

I wouldn't implement everything simultaneously.

🔴 Priority 1 — highest impact
Query intent/router
Adaptive retrieval
Retrieval confidence score
Context builder + strict token budget
Deduplication
Reduce multi-query from fixed 5 → dynamic 1–3
🟠 Priority 2
Better code chunking: method/class/statement hierarchy
Parent-child retrieval
Graph-aware context expansion
Query/embedding/result caching
Retry + controlled concurrency for ingestion
🟡 Priority 3
Evaluate code-specific embedding models
Hybrid lexical + vector retrieval
Query expansion
Context compression
🟢 Experimental
RAPTOR
Agentic retrieval
Self-reflective retrieval

I would not make RAPTOR the next upgrade. Your Neo4j semantic graph already gives you a structural hierarchy that is much more valuable for a Java codebase.

The biggest optimization for your architecture is:

Use Neo4j to understand code structure, Qdrant to understand code meaning, and an adaptive router to decide which one is needed. Don't use both for every question.

That will give you lower latency + fewer embedding/model calls + fewer reranker candidates + substantially fewer LLM tokens, while generally improving code-retrieval precision.